{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Three cities you shall set apart.</b> After explaining the matters of the judges, the king, the priests, and the prophets, he recounts the commandments imposed upon the judges — namely, setting apart cities of refuge, the borders of the land, and the investigation and acceptance of witnesses — and the commandments imposed upon the kings — namely, ״כִּי תֵצֵא לַמִּלְחָמָה״ (Deuteronomy 20:1), ״כִּי תִקְרַב אֶל עִיר״ (Deuteronomy 20:10), and ״כִּי תָצוּר״ (Deuteronomy 20:19) — and that imposed upon the priests and the judges together, namely the matters of the heifer whose neck is broken (Deuteronomy 21:1–9)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:47.193816529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}